  <cac:TenderingProcess>
    
    <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">Nome municipality and Midt-Telemark municipality would like, with this intention notice, to inform the market that they intend to enter into a contract for the procurement of the elements case and archive system with Sikri AS. If the contracting authority does not receive objections by 01.12.2025, a contract will be signed. The background for the procurement is Nome municipality and Midt-Telemark municipality ́s planned entry into the Kongsberg region ́s task partnership for service development and K-ICT. Both municipal councils have made a decision to join the cooperation, and an intention agreement has been signed with the Kongsberg region that describes how the contract shall be carried out. The aim of the cooperation is to strengthen the quality of municipal services, increase competence, reduce vulnerability and facilitate efficient use of resources through sharing competence and joint operations. In order to participate in cooperation with the Kongsberg region, it is a prerequisite that Nome and Midt-Telemark municipalities use the same case and archive system as the other municipalities in the cooperation. The prerequisite for using the same system is connected to the municipality ́s participation in the Kongsberg region Document Centre. This is necessary in order to ensure digital coordination, including effective information flow and interaction across the municipalities, joint routines and processes for document handling and case handling, as well as high quality and compliance with archive and information security requirements. The choice of system follows the established cooperation structure in the region and it is necessary to achieve the planned gains. The procurement is therefore carried out as a direct procurement from the supplier already used by the Kongsberg region, in accordance with the Public Procurement Regulations (FOA) §13-4 letter b.</cbc:Description>
    <cbc:ProcedureCode listName="procurement-procedure-type">neg-wo-call</cbc:ProcedureCode>
    <cac:ProcessJustification>
      <cbc:ProcessReasonCode listName="direct-award-justification">exclusive</cbc:ProcessReasonCode>
      
      <cbc:ProcessReason languageID="ENG">The background for the procurement is Nome municipality and Midt-Telemark municipality ́s planned entry into the Kongsberg region ́s task partnership for service development and K-ICT. 
Both municipal councils have made a decision to join the cooperation, and an intention agreement has been signed with the Kongsberg region that describes how the contract shall be carried out. 
The aim of the cooperation is to strengthen the quality of municipal services, increase competence, reduce vulnerability and facilitate efficient use of resources through sharing competence and joint operations.  

In order to participate in cooperation with the Kongsberg region, it is a prerequisite that Nome and Midt-Telemark municipalities use the same case and archive system as the other municipalities in the cooperation. The prerequisite for using the same system is connected to the municipality ́s participation in the Kongsberg region Document Centre. This is necessary in order to ensure digital coordination, including effective information flow and interaction across the municipalities, joint routines and processes for document handling and case handling, as well as high quality and compliance with archive and information security requirements.

The choice of system follows the established cooperation structure in the region and it is necessary to achieve the planned gains. The procurement is therefore carried out as a direct procurement from the supplier already used by the Kongsberg region, in accordance with the Public Procurement Regulations (FOA) §13-4 letter b.</cbc:ProcessReason>
    </cac:ProcessJustification>
  </cac:TenderingProcess>
